  - **Eager I/O on per-turn paths is a silent regression.** Tier 2.3 originally landed (`8588cab`) with `listResources()` + `experimental_listPrompts()` called inside `buildMcpToolSet`. All tests passed. Advisor asked "is `buildMcpToolSet` per-turn or per-session?" — turned out the agent calls it from 3 per-turn sites (`processMessage`, `processMessageBatchTurn`, `runTaskRequest`). The "passing tests" trap: behaviour was correct, semantics were correct, but I'd added 2 RPC round-trips per server per chat turn for data nothing currently reads. Followup commit `0ed2419` made the discovery lazy via accessor methods. Heuristic for next time: when adding I/O inside any function, grep its call-sites for cardinality (`grep -n functionName src/`). If any call-site is on a hot path, the new I/O must be lazy/optional, not eager. **Promote to a generalizable rule now — the silent-regression flavour is dangerous enough that 1/3 is enough.**
